WEBVTT

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:13.898
Hi, friends. Gani here. This is The Group Chat Pause.

00:00:13.898 --> 00:00:19.797
Sit tall in your chair. Feet flat on the floor.

00:00:19.797 --> 00:00:23.336
Hands resting on your desk. Shoulders soft.

00:00:23.336 --> 00:00:26.875
Take one slow breath with me… and let it go.

00:00:26.875 --> 00:00:35.132
Grown-ups send messages on screens — words that fly from one person to another. You are growing into that world.

00:00:35.132 --> 00:00:44.570
Words on a screen are real words. They can land kindly, and they can land with a sting — just like words out loud.

00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:55.187
Here is the thing about sending: once a message flies, you cannot call it back. It stays sent.

00:00:55.187 --> 00:00:59.905
So before any message flies, there is a pause. It has three beats. Let me show you.

00:00:59.905 --> 00:01:10.522
Beat one: stop. Finger off the button. Nothing has to fly this second. A message can wait.

00:01:10.522 --> 00:01:21.139
Beat two: read it again. Read the words slowly — or ask a grown-up to read them with you. Fresh eyes see more.

00:01:21.139 --> 00:01:31.756
Beat three: ask three questions. Is it kind? Is it true? Do I need to send it now?

00:01:31.756 --> 00:01:41.194
If all three answers are yes, the message may fly. If any answer is no — or even "I'm not sure" — the pause keeps holding.

00:01:41.194 --> 00:01:42.373
Not sending is always allowed. Waiting is always allowed. The pause is never the wrong move.

00:01:42.373 --> 00:01:52.990
And if a message that arrives feels mean, or strange, or makes your stomach feel funny — here is the move: stop.

00:01:52.990 --> 00:02:03.607
Do not reply. Do not send it on to anyone else. Show a grown-up. That is the whole move, and it is a strong one.

00:02:03.607 --> 00:02:11.865
A message can leave a feeling behind — left out, rushed, stung. Those feelings are real, and they are worth saying out loud.

00:02:11.865 --> 00:02:13.045
Kindness cannot be taken back once it is sent — and neither can a sting. That is why the pause comes first.

00:02:13.045 --> 00:02:21.302
Stop. Read it again. Kind, true, now?

00:02:21.302 --> 00:02:27.201
Shoulders soft. Let your body rest.

00:02:27.201 --> 00:02:31.919
Hands down. One more slow breath… and let it go.

00:02:31.919 --> 00:02:37.818
Eyes open. Look around your classroom.

00:02:37.818 --> 00:02:43.716
You're ready for what's next.
